partial-derivative-of-non-abelian-gauge-.conceptual_definition:
The partial derivative of a non-Abelian gauge field component with respect to a spacetime coordinate index $
u$, denoted as $\partial_{
u} A^a_{\mu}$.

partial-derivative-of-non-abelian-gauge-.interpretation:
Physically, this term describes how the gauge potential component $A^a_{\mu}$ changes from one infinitesimal spacetime point to another. The index $
u$ in $\partial_{
u}$ represents the spacetime coordinate derivative, while $A^a_{\mu}$ carries both a Lorentz spacetime index $\mu$ and a gauge group Lie algebra index $a$. In non-Abelian gauge theories, this simple partial derivative lacks gauge covariance on its own, unlike its Abelian counterpart, and must be combined with terms like $g f^{abc} A^b_{\mu} A^c_{
u}$ to construct a gauge-covariant field strength tensor $G^a_{\mu
u}$.
